-- title:
--   Node residues are rational over red(A∩ K)(jmath̃,jmath̃_N)
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, a natural number $N \neq 0$, an algebraically closed field $k$ of characteristic $q$ and a ring homomorphism $\mathrm{red} : A \to k$. Let `data` be modular polynomial data for $q$ (a monic $\Phi \in \mathbb Z[X][Y]$ of degree $\psi(q)$ vanishing at $(j, j_q)$), let `hKr` witness the Kronecker congruence that the reduction of $\Phi$ modulo $q$ equals $(C X^q - X)(C X - X^q)$, and let `hα`, `hβ` witness that the Hecke maps `heckeAlphaBar` and `heckeBetaBar` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ at level $N$ and $q$ are integral ring homomorphisms. Let $P$ be a place specialisation for these data and $R :$ `ProlongationTuple P` a prolongation tuple, so in particular $R$ carries two regular prolongations $R_1, R_2$ of $A$ to $\overline{\mathbb Q}(X_0(Nq))$ with residues in the full modular function field over the residue field of $A$, together with their membership dictionaries and Atkin–Lehner transport. Assume $q \nmid N$, let $K$ be a finite extension of $\mathbb Q$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, let $w$ be a place of `modularFunctionFieldC k N` over $k$ (the field obtained from $k$ by adjoining `jqModC k` and `jqNModC k N` inside $k((q))$), and let $g$ belong to the subring `R.nodeIntegersOver K w`, that is, $g$ lies in `R.nodeIntegers w` and its underlying Laurent series lies in `NodeLocalized.fieldOver (N * q) K`. Then both residues `R.nodeResidue₁ w` and `R.nodeResidue₂ w`, evaluated at the element of `R.nodeIntegers w` underlying $g$, lie in the subfield of `modularFunctionFieldC k N` generated by `jGeomGen k N`, `jNGeomGen k N` and the constants coming from the subfield of $k$ generated by the image of `NodeLocalized.redRestrict red K`, namely of $\mathrm{red}$ composed with the inclusion of `coeffSubring A K` into $A$.
--
--   This is the rationality (descent) step for the two branch residues of a $K$-rational element of the node ring of $X_0(Nq)$: both residues are rational functions of the two moduli generators with coefficients in the residue field of $A \cap K$. It is used in the analysis of when the second residue vanishes at zero in terms of the first, and in the saturation statements for node residues under the order law.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_PlaceSpecialization_ProlongationTuple_nodeResidue_mem_closure_redRestrict.lean

